  "notes": [
   "The 'Required Core: 9 units' heading covers both the two required or-pairs (SSCI 103/SOCI 108 and WSTU 1/SOCI 113) and the 'One course from the following' choice; the stated 9 is recorded on the Required Core block but applies to both blocks together.",
   "List A rule: 'Select three courses from at least two of the following areas (courses must be related to social justice, gender/women, or ethnicity/race'. Courses from Areas 1-4 are recorded once each in a single List A block in order of first appearance. Area 1 (History or Government): ESTU 1/3/5, HIST C1001, C1002, 105, 106, 108, 111, 112, 114, 122, 128, 129, 140, 141, 152, 154, PHIL 117/POLI 7, POLS C1000, POLI 5, POLI 6. Area 2 (Arts and Humanities): AHIS 205A, 205B, 207, 208, 209, ENGL 28, 31, 35, 36, 43, 44, 48, the same HIST courses plus HIST 110, MUSI 112, 113, PHIL 103, PHIL 117/POLI 7. Area 3 (Social Sciences): ANTH 2, 6, 7, 8, 9, COMS 265, 275, ESTU 1/3/5, GEOG 2, GEOG 5, the same HIST courses plus HIST 110, PHIL 117/POLI 7, POLS C1000, POLI 5, POLI 6, PSYC C1000, 102, 108, 110, 112, 115, 116, 117, 119, 125, SOCI 101, 102, 104, 107, 112, 113. Area 4 (Quantitative Reasoning and Research Methods): STAT C1000, PSYC 109A/SOCI 109A. The 'at least two areas' constraint is not captured in the block structure.",
   "A list headed 'Major Preparation:' follows Area 4 with no rule or unit total (AHIS 209, ENGL 42, ENGL 43, ESTU 1, 3, 5, HIST 108, 110, 111, 112, 140, 141, JAPA 1, JAPA 2, PHIL 103, PSYC 109A/SOCI 109A, SOCI 101/101H, SPAN 1/1H, SPAN 2, 3, 4, 52A, 52B, WSTU 1). It appears to duplicate part of the core 'One course from the following' list and is not recorded as a separate block because no rule is given; reviewer should check. All its courses are placed in other blocks.",
   "ITAL 2 and JAPA 2 are printed with a space; the closed list stores them as 'ITAL2' and 'JAPA2' (units not stored). Treated as the same courses (catalog_addition false); catalog prints 5 units each.",
